# grouped_union.tkr — the §9.D Reseed-1 ACCEPT host: the grouped inline-union TYPE capabilities (a) the
# parenthesized type group `(A | B)` in a slice/nested-union position, and (b) the union-mangle
# byte-agreement so a `[](A | B)` names ONE typedef whichever path (decl vs use) emits it. Each scenario
# names itself and asserts its announced value through `run` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself.
# Inert on the seed: the corpus writes no grouped type — these are additive capabilities.

Feature: grouped_union — §9.D grouped inline-union types (Reseed 1, capabilities a + b)

  Scenario: grouped_slice — a `[](Circ | Sq)` slice matches per case (Circ=1, Sq=2 → 12)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario grouped_slice: ok"

  Scenario: byteagree — a `[](Circ | Sq)` built in one fn, consumed through another's signature (len 3)
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario byteagree: ok"

  Scenario: single_collapse — a single-member group `(Circ)` collapses to exactly `Circ`
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario single_collapse: ok"

  Scenario: null_order_mangle — `[](Circ | null)` and `[](null | Circ)` name the same typedef
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario null_order_mangle: ok"
